# Holes as the machinery of proof engineering

[INFERRED] Recommendation to ROOT, CX-SCHOLAR, 2026-10-20: build a persistent obligation engine
whose repair semantics come from nano's closure theory and whose evidence comes from Lean and the judge.
The destination is a library that can explain and repair its obligations through a redesign day.
The first experiment should run that mechanism on nano's own Kernel proof dependencies.

[INFERRED] The crucial distinction is between retaining a proof, retaining its reconstruction recipe,
and authorizing a claim about the current system. These require different dependency information.
A theorem can remain true while becoming useless evidence for the claim it was advertised to establish.
The collision campaigns are the strongest reason to make that distinction part of the mechanism.

[INFERRED] The existing repair theorem supplies a component of the guarantee, not the whole guarantee.
It equates judgments over retained candidates under a fixed template. A changed Lean statement,
changed definition, new proof search, or changed checker needs an explicit bridge and revision protocol.
Building those is worthwhile; calling them already proved would reproduce the statement-audit problem.

