      --pre-compaction [<N>]  Read the pre-compaction span: the messages before a compaction boundary (the context a continued agent lost). Defaults to the FIRST boundary; pass `--pre-compaction <N>` for the Nth (1-based). It sets the window for you, so it excludes the window flags
      --tree                  Instead of the transcript, the message threading — a DAG when messages carry `parent_id`, else a numbered list — then the sub-agent forest, over the whole session. With `--json`, the IR itself: every message carries the same `parent_id`
      --kind <KIND,…>         Only messages of these kinds, comma-separated, as a compact view. `prompt,answer`: what the person said — every typed prompt and `AskUserQuestion` answer with its index and timestamp, printed whole (`--json`: `index, timestamp, kind, text` rows; a window narrows it). `compaction_boundary,compaction_summary`: every compaction seam — trigger, pre-compaction size, the summary that seeded the next window (`--json`: one row per boundary with its `pre_compaction_span`). An affordance — `plan`, `goal`, `schedule`, `background_job`, `subagent_spawn`, `subagent_return`, `skill`, `hook`, `question`, `approval`, `checkpoint`, `branch`, `fork`, `model_change`, or `affordances` for all — lists those rows across harnesses, side stores included (`--json`: `kind, action, index, timestamp, tool, tool_use_id, summary, items, source` rows)
      --summaries             With the compaction kinds: print each summary in full, not just its head
  -h, --help                  Print help

